
How to do the same for Claude Code CLI?

Yes, Google provides an official Android CLI plugin for Claude Code CLI, and you can load all Android Skills directly into Claude Code's skill directories.

1. Install the Official Android CLI Plugin

Google distributes a dedicated Claude Code marketplace plugin in the android-cli-plugin repository that adds the core android-cli skill.
• From your regular terminal:bash
claude plugin marketplace add android/android-cli-plugin
claude plugin install android-cli@android-cli-plugin
Use code with caution.
• Or inside an active claude session:text
/plugin marketplace add android/android-cli-plugin
/plugin install android-cli@android-cli-plugin
Use code with caution.

2. Add All Android Skills to Claude Code

According to the Claude Code Skills documentation and android skills add docs, you can install the specialized skills (such as Jetpack Compose, Navigation 3, or R8 rules) either via the CLI's --agent flag or by symlinking your existing folder:
• Option A: Install directly via android skills add (Recommended).
Specify claude with the --agent flag so Android CLI places the files in Claude Code's directory:bash
android skills add --all --agent=claude
Use code with caution.
• Option B: Symlink your existing skills folder (Zero duplication).
If you already downloaded all skills into ~/.gemini/antigravity/skills for agy and Junie, Claude Code natively resolves symlinked folders inside ~/.claude/skills/:bash
mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills
ln -s ~/.gemini/antigravity/skills/* ~/.claude/skills/
Use code with caution.
(Note: Avoid loading all 30+ skills globally if you want to save context window tokens—you can symlink only the specific skills you need into <projectRoot>/.claude/skills/ instead.)

3. Verify Inside Claude Code

Launch Claude in your Android project and run /skills to confirm android-cli and your imported Android skills appear in the active list.
